What:           /sys/class/switch/touch_pen_detection/state
Date:           October 2026
KernelVersion:  3.10
Description:
                EF67 pen insertion state expected by the stock Android
                android.policy.jar observer. GPIO 79 is read as an input
                with pull-up and 2mA drive, then XORed with the DT flag (1).
                Logical state 0 prints ON; state 1 prints OFF, including
                a trailing newline. This matches S0226114's switch output.
                A change emits a KOBJ_CHANGE uevent with SWITCH_NAME set
                to touch_pen_detection and SWITCH_STATE set to ON or OFF.
                The observer matches
                DEVPATH=/devices/virtual/switch/touch_pen_detection.

                The gpio_switch DT child supplies a plain GPIO number,
                flag, event_mode (1 for switch) and debounce_time (10ms).
                Initial state is sampled during probe. Subsequent edges
                require two equal samples before notification. Both edges
                wake the device; a 500ms wakeup event covers the debounce
                and Android notification interval.

                The input-mode smart_cover device is handled separately
                by the EF67 smart-cover driver. Pen tip coordinates and
                touch configuration are handled separately by the Atmel
                touchscreen driver.
